{title: Crown Him with Many Crowns}
{key: C}
{time: 4/4}
{columns: 2}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C]Crown Him with [**]many [F]crowns[**]
The [C]Lamb u[F]pon His [G]throne[**]
Hark [C]how the [Am]heav'nly [D]anthem [G]drowns[**]
All [G]music [D]but its [G]own[**]
A[C]wake, my [**]soul, and [F]sing[**]
Of [D]Him who [**]died for [G]thee[**]
And [C]hail Him [F]as thy [G]matchless [C]King
Through [F]all e[G]ter–ni[C]ty[**]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[C]Crown Him the [**]Lord of [F]life[**]
Who [C]triumphed [F]o'er the [G]grave[**]
And [C]rose vic[Am]torious [D]in the [G]strife
For [G]those He [D]came to [G]save[**]
His [C]glories [**]now we [F]sing[**]
Who [D]died and [**]rose on [G]high
Who [C]died e[F]ternal [G]life to [C]bring
And [F]lives that [G]death may [C]die[**]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[C]Crown Him the [**]Lord of [F]peace[**]
Whose [C]power a [F]scepter [G]sways[**]
From [C]pole to [Am]pole, that [D]wars may [G]cease
And [G]all be [D]prayer and [G]praise[**]
His [C]reign shall [**]know no [F]end[**]
And [D]round His [**]pierced [G]feet[**]
Fair [C]flowers of [F]para[G]dise ex[C]tend
Their [F]fragrance [G]ever [C]sweet[**].
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
[C]Crown Him the [**]Lord of [F]love[**]
Be[C]hold His [F]hands and [G]side[**]
Those [C]wounds yet [Am]visi[D]ble [G]above
In [G]beauty [D]glori[G]fied[**]
All [C]hail Re[**]deemer, [F]hail[**]
For [D]Thou hast [**]died for [G]me[**]
Thy [C]praise and [F]glory [G]shall not [C]fail
Through[F]out e[G]terni[C]ty[**]
{end_of_verse}
